    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0298" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/475</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-13T08:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                                1918, 8 a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.35 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have carefully examined complete records Emerson acts on his western trip and
                    consider that he used excellent judgment in every case under trying
                    circumstances and I heartily approve all that he did.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
